{"id": 78, "ts": 1780598522.8098645, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s stress\u2011resilience and conscientiousness, but the additional evidence we now have on Candidate\u202fC strengthens his overall fit.\u202fJames confirmed that C \u201cunderstands complicated technology,\u201d indicating solid technical and cognitive competence, and Emily added that C has \u201cexcellent attention skills,\u201d which addresses the attention\u2011and\u2011information\u2011accuracy criterion. Coupled with the facts already on the table\u2014100\u202f% reliability, calmness in crisis, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and a positive crew atmosphere\u2014C now demonstrates a well\u2011rounded profile across the most safety\u2011critical dimensions.\nWhile C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric attitude, and limited willingness for further education remain concerns, they appear less likely to jeopardize operational safety than B\u2019s documented grumpiness, uncooperativeness, and weak numeric memory, which could directly affect crew coordination and flight\u2011planning accuracy. Therefore, I continue to recommend **Candidate\u202fC** as the best overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
