{"id": 82, "ts": 1780598566.3072977, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I acknowledge Sarah\u2019s compelling summary of Candidate\u202fC\u2019s strengths\u2014100\u202f% reliability, calmness in crisis, rapid correct decisions, solid technical understanding, and excellent attention skills. Those attributes are indeed vital for long\u2011distance operations. However, the concerns around C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric attitude, and limited willingness to pursue further education strike at the core of crew cooperation and adaptability, both essential for safe, multi\u2011crew environments. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB demonstrates strong stress resilience, high conscientiousness, and accurate weather assessment, all of which directly support operational reliability and decision quality on long routes. While B\u2019s weak numeric memory and occasional nasty remarks are not ideal, they are more specific and potentially mitigable through procedural safeguards and crew\u2011resource\u2011management training than the broader interpersonal deficits evident in C. Therefore, I maintain my recommendation for **Candidate\u202fB** as the better overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
