{"id": 86, "ts": 1780598602.413776, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I concur with James\u2019s assessment that Candidate\u202fB remains the strongest overall fit. While Candidate\u202fC brings impressive reliability and calmness, his difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric attitude, and lack of willingness to pursue further education raise serious doubts about crew cooperation and adaptability\u2014both non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011distance multi\u2011crew flights. Candidate\u202fA, despite his ability to anticipate danger and see complex connections, is described as unfriendly and has unhealthy eating habits, which signal potential issues with operational reliability, stress resilience, and crew cohesion. Candidate\u202fD, although technically adept and responsible, is noted as moody and a loner, suggesting possible challenges in maintaining a constructive cockpit environment under pressure. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s strong stress handling, conscientiousness, accurate weather assessment, and calm demeanor directly address the core safety criteria, and his communication tone issues appear manageable through training. Therefore, I maintain my vote for **Candidate\u202fB**."}
